#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
DiscRipper - archival-grade optical disc ripper for Windows.

Rips audio CDs, DVDs, Blu-rays and data discs from any optical drive Windows
can see (internal, USB-A, USB-C) and stores them as efficiently as possible
with no quality loss by default:

    Audio CD  -> FLAC (lossless compression) via cyanrip, with AccurateRip
                 verification, MusicBrainz metadata and cover art.
    DVD/BD    -> Lossless MKV remux via MakeMKV (no re-encode), or full
                 decrypted disc backup. Optional lossy compression stage
                 (x264/x265/AV1, hardware encoders) via ffmpeg/HandBrake.
    Data disc -> Bit-exact ISO image (raw read, hashed in one pass) or
                 verified file copy.

Run with no arguments for the interactive wizard. Run "discripper.py --help"
for the full CLI. Run "discripper.py setup" to install the ripping engines.

Requires Python 3.11+. External engines (installed by "setup"):
    MakeMKV (makemkvcon), cyanrip, ffmpeg/ffprobe, HandBrakeCLI (optional).
"""

